AUPTIME(1)                 General Commands Manual                 AUPTIME(1)

NAME
       auptime - actual uptime

SYNOPSIS
       ./auptime

DESCRIPTION
       auptime (actual uptime) displays the time since boot that Linux has
       spent awake, in days, hours, minutes and seconds. Time spent in
       suspend is excluded. Normal idle time still counts; looking busy
       is not required.

       Standard Linux uptime includes suspend. auptime does not give
       your laptop credit for sleeping through the weekend.

BUILD
       Requires Linux, a C compiler and make.

       make

EXAMPLE
       $ ./auptime
       up 2d 03:04:05

NOTES
       The time is read from clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC). No daemon,
       saved state or root privileges are required.

       CLOCK_MONOTONIC excludes suspend; CLOCK_BOOTTIME includes it.
       Manual wall-clock changes do not affect the reported time.
       Gradual clock frequency adjustments can affect its rate.

CLEAN
       make clean

SEE ALSO
       uptime(1), clock_gettime(2)
